# Bacillus anthracis MLVA-31 as bundled by MLVAbank, in the order of the source table: the
# eight MLVA-8 loci of Keim et al. 2000, then seventeen bams loci of Lista et al. 2006, then
# six vntr loci of Van Ert et al. 2007. The locus ids are the short names and the label column
# of markers.tsv keeps the full MLVAbank identifier, which encodes the reference values.
#
# bams07 is in the source table but not in this scheme. The table holds 32 loci, of which
# bams07 alone carries an extra footnote mark, and 32 less that one locus is the 31 of the
# panel name; the remaining seventeen bams loci are also exactly the set of Lista et al. The
# locus itself is sound, giving one product of its published 1017 bp in the reference, so it
# can be added by uncommenting the two lines below and the matching line in markers.tsv.
#
# The expected size is a window from the reference size less 250 bp, floored at 60, to the
# reference size plus 450 bp, wide enough for a large allele range. It only bounds the search
# and does not affect allele calls, and it can be tightened per locus from published ranges.
